{"parentUuid":"5a8a63c1-839b-4e58-b788-840d2ae89312","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt3AdTVpQhC5Lj73dY8n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #91 finding on #483 is fixed and resolved, and a new fix for first-time users is up as #485.\n\n**Finding on #483 (reused changeset names).** The finding was right. I kept the oldest PR for a reused name, but the file that exists now is the newest addition. It now keeps the newest. A new test fails with the old code, and the full checks pass. The commit is signed and the finding is marked resolved on the trail.\n\n**New fix, #485 (draft).** I ran Callisto on a fresh two-crate repo as a new user would: init, add, status, version, then the PR body.\n- **What worked:** the flow was clear, and the changelog and PR body read well. \"Check the bump\" correctly flagged a deliberately mismatched Breaking note.\n- **What was wrong:** the first release PR said \"Changed, not releasing: source changed since the last release\" for a package that had never been released. Every untagged package got that false alarm.\n- **Fix:** packages with no tag are skipped in that finding, with a test that fails without the fix. The checks, including `just workflow-contracts`, exit 0.\n- **Conflict with #483:** the two PRs overlap in one paragraph of `docs/architecture/versioning.md`. The code merges cleanly, so whichever lands second needs a one-line doc fix, which I'll do.\n\nAwaiting you: reviews on #483 and #485, and merging #468.\n\nneeds input: review #483 and #485."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":289559,"output_tokens":469,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":516,"ephemeral_5m_input_to