{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"e28f729bb61c96cb1c5af5741366fc9908aa8c430492264c97d8f7c24e6f71e1","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"You're right. I wrote these changesets carelessly, and my own memory notes say to keep them short, plain and free of backstory. I'll go through them. The two problems I can already see:\n\n- **Wording:** my entries explain implementation (\"read from the merge commits with one `git log`\") and read like debugging notes, not release notes.\n- **Granularity:** the 0.19.0 changelog has 13 entries, and most are fix-ups to features that haven't shipped yet. A user doesn't need \"headlines starting with a code span are now titled correctly\" for a feature they've never seen.\n\nI'm starting with the two PRs I own. #485 fixes a finding that is itself new in 0.19.0, so it needs no changeset at all."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TSVzjKS1evrJLU47dkGfv1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git rm -q .changeset/unreleased-needs-a-tag.md && git commit -S -q -m \"chore: drop the changeset; the finding it fixes has not been released\" && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -1; git log -1 --format=%h","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XVi7DAzUnQ6KvyaAbxHbfa","name":"EnterWorktree","input":{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/change-pr-links"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
