{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":8710,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"5498752b-533a-4418-9618-03f430fdd80c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt4fk53h4ZVraqgxbmPx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 0.19.0 changeset text is now rewritten in #486, #483's changeset names the link, and #485 has none. #486 and #483 are open as drafts, with CI not yet run.\n\nYou were right that the text never named the feature. My #483 changeset said the PR \"says which pull request added\" each change, with no mention of a link, where it shows or why it helps. It now reads: *\"The release PR now links each change to the pull request that introduced it. The link, such as `#123`, sits next to the change, so you can open the discussion and review behind a line without searching for it.\"*\n\n**#486 (all pending 0.19.0 changesets):** 13 entries become 7, each saying what changed, why it helps and what to do. I folded in the fix-ups to features that haven't shipped, since a user never sees those. I also tightened the `--emit-preview` entry, which said \"facts\" for what is really a JSON file. `AGENTS.md` now asks for why it matters to the user, and says a fix to unreleased work gets no changeset. Bumps stay minor.\n\n**#485:** I dropped its changeset, because it fixes a finding that is itself new in 0.19.0.\n\n**Your call on the text.** Please read the seven entries in #486, since that is what users will see. If any still reads like something a user couldn't picture, say which and I'll fix it.\n\n**Conflict note.** #483 and #485 both touch one doc paragraph in `docs/architecture/versioning.md`, so the second to merge needs a one-line fix from me.\n\nneeds input: read the seven entries in #486, then review #483, #485 and #486."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":318154,"output_tokens":513,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"