{"parentUuid":"654cc38b-d59c-41ce-81b9-dee8885d1e35","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt4qRye1fNW2Px1Fvm3N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1305,"cache_read_input_tokens":319486,"output_tokens":2025,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1142},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1305,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2025,"cache_read_input_tokens":319486,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1305},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11015,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e2d2f089-3bf8-43c9-8fa9-2eddf9fe66e6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgt4qRfnyH7bZ5yUaFg1Y","requestRef":"557b5577-cbed-41d4-9721-e0db7ebc5028","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"58d1cf9e-df9d-45b4-b659-cc1ee39ff2a8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:30:40.194Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"58d1cf9e-df9d-45b4-b659-cc1ee39ff2a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt4qRye1fNW2Px1Fvm3N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll make no more edits until we agree on the goal. Rewriting the seven files again would be the same mistake.\n\n**What the work is.** A changeset is the only thing a Callisto user reads about a release. Each entry should let someone who has never seen the code answer three questions in a few seconds:\n- **What is it?** Name the thing they'll see.\n- **Why do they care?**\n- **Do they need to do anything?**\n\n**Why I keep missing, from what happened here**\n- **Written last, from my own head.** I wrote each changeset as an afterthought, after I'd built the feature, so I described how it works (\"one `git log`\", \"facts\") instead of what a user sees.\n- **The rule is abstract.** AGENTS.md says \"lead with what the user sees now\", with no example of good and bad text, and nothing checks it. I wrote to satisfy the checks that exist.\n- **I skipped our own tooling.** My memory says to route PR and commit narration through the courier agents. I didn't for changesets. The courier changeset agent exists for exactly this.\n- **Nobody read the output as a user.** The release PR showed 13 entries, and I never read them as a first-time user would.\n- **Fixes to unreleased work got entries.** That is why 13 entries became 7.\n\n**How I'd set us up so it sticks**\n1. **A concrete shape in AGENTS.md.** One lead sentence that names the visible thing, optional short bullets, an optional action line, and a few before-and-after examples taken from this episode. A shape plus examples is harder to ignore than a principle.\n2. **A reader check before every changeset.** Could someone who hasn't seen the code say what the feature is, why it helps and what to do? I'd run the courier changeset agent, and I'd read the draft as a user.\n3. **Review at the right moment.** Read the rendered release PR body before merging it. It is the first view of what users will see.\n4. **Granularity rule.** One entry per user-visible feature, edited as the feature evolves. A fix to something unreleased gets no entry.\n5. **Optional, and your call:** a soft warning in Callisto itself for changesets that are too long or describe mechanism. It would help your users write good changesets too. I'm wary of it, because heuristics get brittle and you've warned against over-engineering.\n\nQuestions for you:\n- **Audience:** is it a Callisto CLI user upgrading, or also people who script it? That changes how much detail the bullets carry.\n- **Length:** do you want a hard target, such as a lead of about 20 words and bullets of about 8?\n- **Lint:** is item 5 something you want, or leave it out?\n\nneeds input: answers to those three, or tell me which of items 1 to 4 you want first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1305,"cache_read_input_tokens":319486,"output_tokens":2025,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1142},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1305,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2025,"cache_read_input_tokens":319486,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1305},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e2d2f089-3bf8-43c9-8fa9-2eddf9fe66e6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgt4qRfnyH7bZ5yUaFg1Y","requestRef":"557b5577-cbed-41d4-9721-e0db7ebc5028","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","ty