{"parentUuid":"8a5967a8-2741-449c-b63b-6707f790f2da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtE7TPDZXtwC1ydfwVXS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":324976,"output_tokens":1785,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":983},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1785,"cache_read_input_tokens":324976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7760,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"8ed23a22-e82a-40b5-bde5-7255753fbf6a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgtE7T5cWYzg6AUfvv2xb","requestRef":"8864a363-ca57-4728-93b0-66409142b1a6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"289e6d21-306b-457e-a1d5-b444977b0f07","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:32:16.620Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"289e6d21-306b-457e-a1d5-b444977b0f07","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtE7TPDZXtwC1ydfwVXS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood. We write principles and judgment, not length limits, and we fit the entry to what the reader needs.\n\n**What I'd write down**\n- **Audience first.** Each entry says what it means for someone upgrading, scripting or setting up, using sections when there is enough to say and one sentence when there isn't.\n- **Scannable first, detail on demand.** A lead line gives the value, bullets give the specifics, and sub-bullets hold the depth for people who want it.\n- **One entry per outcome, not per PR.** The last PR of a feature writes or updates the entry. A PR that isn't user-visible, or fixes something unreleased, gets no changeset.\n- **Review means reading the rendered release PR as a user.** Don't just check that the files pass.\n\n**Worked example (draft, nothing written to a file).** Here is what 0.19.0's release PR work could be as one entry, in place of five:\n\n```\nA release PR that tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n**What you see**\n- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line and linking its pull request (`#123`)\n- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, and packages that changed but aren't in this release\n- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n\n**Scripting**\n- `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n- `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n  - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n**Upgrading**\n- Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n```\n\nWith that, 0.19.0 would be three entries: this one, the grouped changelog layout, and the `--cwd` change.\n\n**Tradeoffs.** One big entry loses the per-feature split in the changelog, but the bump is the same. It does need someone to own the entry across PRs, and I'd make that the final PR of the feature.\n\n**Open question for you:** do the section names (What you see, Scripting, Upgrading) feel right as a convention, or should they vary by entry?\n\nneeds input: your reaction to the example, and whether the section names should be a convention or free-form."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":324976,"output_tokens":1785,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":983},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1785,"cache_read_input_tokens":324976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8ed23a22-e82a-40b5-bde5-7255753fbf6a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgtE7T5cWYzg6AUfvv2xb","requestRef":"8864a363-ca57-4728-93b0-66409142b1a6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1078f78b-9af6-4e73-ba60-2917b4a0bf84","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:32:22.266Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","ent